SOCIAL MEDIA CHECK LIST

| Do's                                                                                     | Don'ts                                                                                 |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Verify before sharing - Check facts using reliable sources before posting news or claims | Don't share personal info - Avoid posting addresses, phone numbers, or exact locations |
| Use privacy settings - Set profiles to private and control who sees your posts           | Don't accept unknown friend requests - Be cautious of strangers or suspicious accounts |
| Think before posting - Consider long-term impact on future jobs/education                | Don't engage in cyberbullying - Never harass, troll, or spread hate online             |
| Report inappropriate content - Use platform tools to flag spam, abuse, or fake news      | Don't overshare daily routines - Avoid posting real-time locations or schedules        |
| Take digital breaks - Limit screen time to maintain focus on studies                     | Don't use weak passwords - Avoid simple passwords across multiple social accounts      |


Pro Tip: Follow the 60-second rule - wait 60 seconds before posting anything questionable to avoid rash decisions that could impact your VIT Bhopal academic/professional reputation.
